assembly as a draft. Verify that every claim traces to your own evidence and that the recommendation is one you can defend.","rail_action":"represent"},{"id":"cat531_supplement_5_8_completion_closes_decision","pattern":"completed_brief_treated_as_closed","description":"Treating a polished, complete brief as a closed decision with no stated condition that would change the recommendation","trigger":"learner omits what evidence would overturn the conclusion","feedback":"Name what could change the recommendation. A decision that cannot say what would change its mind is an assertion, not an inspectable judgment.","rail_action":"ask"}],"content_version":{"content_version":"a5fd95ba158f0685142fe4b9729dcf07444be5bbaf2794cd25156d9c39357d24","algorithm":"sha256-mdx+meta+practice+misconceptions-v1","parts":["mdx","meta","practice","misconceptions"]}}